Laser annealing is a precision thermal process used in semiconductor manufacturing to modify material properties through controlled laser energy. It enables localized heating, supports dopant activation, and helps minimize thermal damage to surrounding structures. These capabilities are increasingly important as chip manufacturers develop advanced process technologies and more complex semiconductor devices.

Demand is supported by investments in semiconductor fabrication, power electronics, memory devices, and advanced packaging. Equipment manufacturers are also developing laser systems with improved temperature control, processing precision, and throughput to address the requirements of next-generation semiconductor production.

